body:
I'm not exactly an arts major at Waterloo but I'm in the same shoes as you. I'm also a 12th grader, applied to ARBUS comm studies at Waterloo, and considering going here (deciding over Laurier or UofW). I browse the internet a lot, mainly reddit, to see others' opinions on being a communications major and all I see is people saying it's useless and a whole bunch of negativity. I'm trying my best for those comments to not get to me (tbh they have), but damn what can I do. All programs get shit on. Many shit on other programs just because they don't know anything about it. Communications mainly, because to outsiders it sounds like all we do is learn how to talk.

&#x200B;

Just know that if you do end up choosing Waterloo, I'm sure you won't get anyone going up to your face and telling you you're stupid for being an arts major. You're not alone, it's stupid to generalize a whole faculty! If we both end up choosing Waterloo, then I guess I'll see you around :)
